WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.960 --> 00:00:02.610
- [Narrator] Russia has
been amassing troops

00:00:02.610 --> 00:00:05.004
near its border with Ukraine for weeks.

00:00:05.004 --> 00:00:05.980
(blades whirring)

00:00:05.980 --> 00:00:07.750
The prospect of a possible attack

00:00:07.750 --> 00:00:09.520
has triggered tense negotiations

00:00:09.520 --> 00:00:11.130
and diplomatic efforts

00:00:11.130 --> 00:00:12.930
as the US and NATO has been trying

00:00:12.930 --> 00:00:16.155
to discourage Russia from
taking military action.

00:00:16.155 --> 00:00:17.880
- Economics are very
difficult for Ukraine as well

00:00:17.880 --> 00:00:20.106
being almost surrounded.

00:00:20.106 --> 00:00:24.606
(Sergei speaking in foreign language)

00:00:28.250 --> 00:00:29.920
- [Narrator] The stakes are high.

00:00:29.920 --> 00:00:31.430
The West has threatened sanctions

00:00:31.430 --> 00:00:34.010
and military deployment by NATO.

00:00:34.010 --> 00:00:36.460
While Moscow says it doesn't
plan to invade the country,

00:00:36.460 --> 00:00:39.244
it wants to have a say
in Ukraine's future.

00:00:39.244 --> 00:00:42.550
Since Ukraine was invaded
by Russian troops in 2014,

00:00:42.550 --> 00:00:44.310
it has strengthened its own military

00:00:44.310 --> 00:00:47.560
and many Ukrainians say
they're ready to fight.

00:00:47.560 --> 00:00:49.620
But what happens now also depends

00:00:49.620 --> 00:00:51.360
on whether tensions between the US

00:00:51.360 --> 00:00:53.113
and Russia keep escalating.

00:00:55.350 --> 00:00:56.980
Moscow began stationing troops

00:00:56.980 --> 00:01:00.090
and military equipment near
Ukraine in December of last year

00:01:00.090 --> 00:01:02.920
as was documented by satellite images.

00:01:02.920 --> 00:01:06.130
By early January, 100,000
troops were amassed not far

00:01:06.130 --> 00:01:08.050
from Ukraine's border.

00:01:08.050 --> 00:01:11.340
President Putin has long
claimed ties to Ukraine,

00:01:11.340 --> 00:01:13.120
a former Soviet Republic,

00:01:13.120 --> 00:01:14.700
and has repeatedly indicated

00:01:14.700 --> 00:01:17.310
that he wants it back
under Russia's influence.

00:01:17.310 --> 00:01:20.010
- In recent years, Ukraine
has sought to join NATO

00:01:20.010 --> 00:01:21.270
and the EU.

00:01:21.270 --> 00:01:23.080
These blocs are not offering membership

00:01:23.080 --> 00:01:25.330
but Putin has accused
them of turning Ukraine

00:01:25.330 --> 00:01:28.567
into an anti-Russia on
his country's borders.

00:01:28.567 --> 00:01:33.234
(Vladimir speaking in foreign language)

00:01:37.320 --> 00:01:39.010
- [Narrator] Ukraine's
president, Volodymyr Zelensky,

00:01:39.010 --> 00:01:41.770
said NATO has an interest
in supporting Kiev

00:01:41.770 --> 00:01:43.980
to contain any fallout of a Russian attack

00:01:43.980 --> 00:01:45.490
that could affect its member states,

00:01:45.490 --> 00:01:47.193
especially in Eastern Europe.

00:01:48.980 --> 00:01:50.720
- In the past, Russia has resorted

00:01:50.720 --> 00:01:54.130
to military action to keep Ukraine close.

00:01:54.130 --> 00:01:56.360
When the country ousted
its pro-Russian president

00:01:56.360 --> 00:01:58.970
in a revolution in early 2014,

00:01:58.970 --> 00:02:02.053
Moscow responded by seizing
Crimea in southern Ukraine.

00:02:03.020 --> 00:02:04.590
That war and other conflicts

00:02:04.590 --> 00:02:06.850
involving pro-Russian
separatists in recent years

00:02:06.850 --> 00:02:09.060
have fueled a wave of
Ukrainian nationalism,

00:02:09.060 --> 00:02:11.180
according to some socialists.

00:02:11.180 --> 00:02:12.890
- Before 2014, a lot of people felt

00:02:12.890 --> 00:02:14.420
quite positive about Russia.

00:02:14.420 --> 00:02:17.160
Now a lot of people in
Ukraine see it as an invader.

00:02:17.160 --> 00:02:18.740
- [Narrator] 1/3 of respondents in a poll

00:02:18.740 --> 00:02:21.030
late last year indicated
they would take up arms

00:02:21.030 --> 00:02:23.143
to defend the country if it was attacked.

00:02:24.180 --> 00:02:26.210
This woman has been
training as a reservist

00:02:26.210 --> 00:02:28.900
in the Ukrainian army for 18 months.

00:02:28.900 --> 00:02:32.120
- I came here to the
Territory Defense Forces

00:02:32.120 --> 00:02:36.350
to have the skills to use the gun

00:02:36.350 --> 00:02:39.260
to defend myself, to defend my family

00:02:39.260 --> 00:02:42.373
from possible Russian aggression.

00:02:43.321 --> 00:02:44.810
(guns clicking)

00:02:44.810 --> 00:02:46.580
- [Narrator] Ukraine, which
is the largest country

00:02:46.580 --> 00:02:47.910
in the region apart from Russia,

00:02:47.910 --> 00:02:49.770
said it's been strengthening its military

00:02:49.770 --> 00:02:51.540
and prepared its people to fight.

00:02:51.540 --> 00:02:52.900
- There's also a fighting spirit

00:02:52.900 --> 00:02:55.100
that has improved since 2014.

00:02:55.100 --> 00:02:57.120
People who are ready to
defend their country,

00:02:57.120 --> 00:02:58.490
not only in the army

00:02:58.490 --> 00:03:01.030
but also volunteers, people bringing help

00:03:01.030 --> 00:03:02.880
to those who are ready to fight.

00:03:02.880 --> 00:03:04.350
- [Narrator] Still,
there are also residents

00:03:04.350 --> 00:03:05.680
in Ukraine's border regions

00:03:05.680 --> 00:03:08.020
who say they feel more
closely tied to Russia

00:03:08.020 --> 00:03:09.673
than the West.

00:03:09.673 --> 00:03:13.430
(Vladimir speaking in foreign language)

00:03:13.430 --> 00:03:15.690
- [Narrator] The US and NATO
have offered their support,

00:03:15.690 --> 00:03:17.953
although Western allies remain divided.

00:03:18.800 --> 00:03:21.390
The White House has previously
ruled out sending troops

00:03:21.390 --> 00:03:22.600
on the ground in Ukraine

00:03:22.600 --> 00:03:25.010
but has sent weaponry and
other equipment to the country,

00:03:25.010 --> 00:03:28.360
having approved $200
million in such assistance.

00:03:28.360 --> 00:03:30.640
- If they actually do what
they're capable of doing

00:03:30.640 --> 00:03:32.910
with the force amassed on the border,

00:03:32.910 --> 00:03:35.910
it is going to be a disaster for Russia.

00:03:35.910 --> 00:03:38.740
- [Narrator] Other NATO members
also sent arms to Ukraine,

00:03:38.740 --> 00:03:40.230
while the bloc increased deployments

00:03:40.230 --> 00:03:43.530
of troops and equipment in
its eastern member states.

00:03:43.530 --> 00:03:45.760
But some European countries like Germany

00:03:45.760 --> 00:03:48.240
and Italy were reluctant
to take stronger action,

00:03:48.240 --> 00:03:50.240
partly because they are major importers

00:03:50.240 --> 00:03:51.653
of energy from Russia.

00:03:52.530 --> 00:03:54.250
- Russia will be held accountable.

00:03:54.250 --> 00:03:56.150
- [Narrator] So far, the
Biden administration's

00:03:56.150 --> 00:03:57.820
main strategy has been the threat

00:03:57.820 --> 00:04:00.090
of crippling economic sanctions on Russia,

00:04:00.090 --> 00:04:02.010
which hasn't backed down on its demands

00:04:02.010 --> 00:04:05.060
and continued military
activity along the border.

00:04:05.060 --> 00:04:09.393
(pensive music)

